A_047 - If you find yourself struggling to solve a problem while sitting in front of your computer because your mind can't quite grasp it, try tackling the problem while you're eating. You'll find the solution to that problem in a flash. This happens because the computer's electromagnetic waves influence our reasoning, complicating the process of problem-solving. This is a little-studied aspect of computer operation, but it does exist. The same thing happens when we approach a spinning washing machine, an electric car, or a running hair dryer. The object's electromagnetic field interferes with our mind.